elements.description:
`Draft.run`: meta → removals (cascade to descendants, relations, flow steps, layout) → element/relation/flow upserts → integrity checks → clean-up of data references lost by the change set (with warnings) → the same `integrityProblems` check the store runs on load, so no change set can persist a model that would not load again. Errors are collected and thrown together as one `ChangeError` naming each entry, with did-you-mean suggestions.

With code access (the server host hands the store `StaleLinks.access`), code ref paths are normalized against the repository (an absolute path inside it becomes repo-relative, one outside is an error) and every ref a change set writes is sealed:
- same location and digest as the stored ref: kept as is, without reading the file, so resending a list never accepts drift;
- a digest at a new location: a claim that the code there is the sealed text, verified against the file; the change set is rejected when it is not (this is how repair's moves are checked);
- no digest: sealed afresh to the current text, which is how a ref re-sent in `addCodeRefs` accepts edited code.

A ref that is stale already when written comes back as a warning.

